{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"anchor":"Type-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Type Methods"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are one failure mode; the other is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — an entity an app holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fresh installs, two singletons have "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"([E]) -> [E]"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}]},{"text":"The determinism requirement","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other’s, and after sync ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" rows are gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It must also be idempotent — ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(collapse(rows))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs as ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This is checked with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in debug builds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","type":"heading","text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each should contain","type":"text"}]},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"reference"},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"preferring"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapses rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" down to one, keeping the winner of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"choose"},{"type":"text","text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","title":"byID(preferring:)","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","type":"topic","title":"EntityDB","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"text":" that reads and writes any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistableModel"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistableModel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","kind":"symbol","title":"PersistableModel"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","title":"EntityCollapse","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","title":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence"}}}